[size=4][b]What[/b][/size]

[size=3]Makes every headstone and grave fence count as quality 30, whatever it's made of, and stops a body's white skulls from limiting the grave.[/size]

[list]
[*][size=3][b]Modify Graves[/b] (on by default): every headstone and fence is worth 30. A grave with both is worth 60 before the body is counted.[/size]
[*][size=3][b]Ignore Body Skull Limit[/b] (on by default): in the base game a grave can never be worth more than the body's white skulls. This removes that limit. Red skulls still count against the grave. Turn it off to keep the base game's limit.[/size]
[*][size=3][b]Modify Decorations[/b] (off by default): graveyard decorations such as columbariums, flowerbeds and lawns are worth 30 each as well.[/size]
[*][size=3]No unlock needed. New and existing graves use these values when the game recalculates their quality.[/size]
[*][size=3]On a new save the grave changes switch on once you've had your first talk with the bishop and collected your tools. A notice tells you while they're waiting.[/size]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Other mods of mine you might like[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/62]Where's Ma' Storage[/url] — shared inventory across workstations. Carrying around grave-item sets becomes much less painful.[/size]
[*][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/86]Decomp Delight[/url] — element tags on every researched item's tooltip for efficient alchemy.[/size]
[*][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/57]Queue Everything[/url] — queue morgue-table crafts. Per-workbench auto-craft supports the morgue, packing, and autopsy tables.[/size]
[*][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/60]I Build Where I Want[/url] — place grave structures anywhere, not just in pre-defined plots.[/size]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

[size=3]If you installed the required [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/79]Graveyard Keeper BepInEx 5 Pack[/url] and this mod is configurable, press F1 in-game to open the config interface.[/size]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper/mods/79][size=3]Graveyard Keeper BepInEx 5 Pack at Graveyard Keeper Nexus - Mods and community (nexusmods.com)[/size][/url]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[size=3]Built and tested against the latest Windows Steam build of Graveyard Keeper. Other storefronts and platforms aren't extensively tested — should generally work, but YMMV.[/size]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[size=3]Installation using Vortex is the recommended installation method. If you wish to install manually, extract the contents of the mod archive into:[/size]

[code]...\steamapps\common\Graveyard Keeper\BepInEx[/code]

